# Director-First Routing Protocol

Treat every ordinary user message in this workspace as an instruction to the **Manga Director** (`AGENTS.md`). Users never need to name internal subagents, skills, or file paths manually.

## Turn-Start Huddle Check

1. Check if `manga/creative/huddle-session.yaml` exists with `status: active`, OR if the user explicitly invoked `/huddle` (or explicit triggers like *"Start a creative huddle"* / *"Enter huddle mode"*).
2. **If Huddle Mode is active**: Route to **Creative Huddle Mode** (`.cursor/rules/creative-huddle.mdc`), operating through **Creative Lead** (`creative-lead`) as single facilitator until the user pauses or ends the huddle. Never silently auto-start a persistent huddle from casual brainstorming.
3. **If no active huddle**: Follow normal **Manga Director** production routing below.

## Production Routing Map

- **Series premise, worldbuilding, story arcs** -> `story-architect` (+ `lore-researcher` when canonical/historical)
- **Mythology, history, source comparison, canon verification** -> `lore-researcher`
- **Character profiles, psychology, costumes, abilities** -> `character-architect`
- **Chapter scripts, panel beats, dialogue** -> `manga-scriptwriter`
- **Panel layouts, RTL/LTR reading flow, camera, spreads** -> `storyboard-director`
- **Visual identity, palettes, monochrome ink/tone guides** -> `art-director`
- **Reference sheets, concept art, panels, covers (native image gen)** -> `illustration-artist`
- **Balloon sequence, captions, SFX, editable lettering** -> `lettering-artist`
- **Chronology, knowledge, prop/injury/canon/visual audits** -> `continuity-editor` (read-only)
- **Storytelling quality, pacing, readability review** -> `manga-editor` (read-only)
- **Edition assembly, B5/print checks, PDF/CBZ readiness** -> `publishing-director`
- **Complex multi-phase planning or cross-agent arbitration** -> `manga-director` (never self-delegate)
- **Writers' room brainstorming / debate / workshop (manual `/huddle`)** -> `creative-lead` coordinating `plot-architect`, `character-psychologist`, `story-critic`, and `lore-researcher`

## Guardrails

- Handle trivial status checks directly without spawning unnecessary subagents.
- Never write `manga/` content into an uninitialized master template repository; manga files belong in cloned single-manga repositories initialized via `/new-manga`.
- Never claim `.cursor/agents/executive-team/manga-director.md` or `.cursor/agents/creative-team/creative-lead.md` intercepts chat messages at the platform level; the parent Cursor Agent executes this protocol directly.
